# AGENTS.md

@REPO@: @DESCRIPTION_SENTENCE@ It follows the
[Kokeb Labs engineering standard](https://github.com/kokeb-labs/.github/blob/main/standards/README.md)
(agents: `standards/agents.md`, libraries:
`standards/library.md`).

## Layout

- `inc/@ROOT@/`: the public headers, one include root (`#include "@ROOT@/<Header>.h"`), PascalCase file
  names. `Version.h` is generated from `Version.h.in`.
- `tests/host/`: host tests; `tests/docs/`: every code block on the site; `tests/install_consumer/`.
- `docs/`: the site. `examples/<platform>/`: the only platform code; `examples/host/` always exists and runs in
  the host tests.
- `cmake/xmpl100_build_settings.cmake`: the only place the version is set.

## Layer rules

- Platform-free: no RTOS, no vendor SDK, no global mutable state, no heap, exceptions, RTTI, `std::function`,
  `std::string` or `printf`. A helper that needs a lock or a clock takes it as a parameter.
- Code in `namespace xmpl100`; no macros that leak (`MIN`, `MAX`); no header path shared with another repository.
- Every fallible call returns `Result<T>`; `Error` keeps the base names and values, library values from 16.
- Public and protected methods PascalCase, private camelBack, members `snake_case_`, constants `kPascalCase`.

## Build and test on the host

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DXMPL100_BUILD_TESTS=ON
cmake --build build --parallel && ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

## Docs checks

```bash
kokeb-docs gen && kokeb-docs check && mkdocs build -f _config/mkdocs.yml --strict -d /tmp/site
```

## Definition of done

`standards/agents.md#definition-of-done`: one change; standard followed or deviation named; every check above
passes locally (the `verify` skill); tests for new behaviour including failure paths; docs and Doxygen updated;
`CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]`; CI green including `CI gate / gate`.

## Rules specific to this repo

- No attribution lines anywhere: no `Co-Authored-By:` trailers, no "Generated with" footers.
- Work on a `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `ci/` or `chore/` branch; never push to `main`, force-push, merge or change
  settings.
